    {
        "text": "History records that out of a sense the war between the Draco and Aslan had become far too protracted and bitter, the final King Gaeil signed a peace treaty.",
        "tag": "name",
        "value": "Plain-Dressed Bard"
    },
    {
        "text": "Legends say he opted to melt down his soldiers' weapons as a sign of his determination, but his subjects could hardly accept such a defeat. Thus they conspired to revolt, and assassinated the monarch.",
        "tag": "name",
        "value": "Plain-Dressed Bard"
    },
    {
        "text": "But just as you've referenced in many a speech, a single assassination is not enough to extinguish the Red Dragon's whole bloodline.",
        "tag": "name",
        "value": "Plain-Dressed Bard"
    },
    {
        "tag": "character",
        "name": "avg_npc_727_1#1$1"
    },
    {
        "text": "No matter how the Victorians write the history books, they cannot change what facts we've seen with our own eyes.",
        "tag": "name",
        "value": "Earl of Warwick"
    },
    {
        "text": "The Aslan promised to share Victoria's kingship with the Draco, yet didn't hand over the crown for nearly a century.",
        "tag": "name",
        "value": "Earl of Warwick"
    },
    {
        "text": "With the lions' ambitions so conspicuous to this point, I wonder. Six blade marks stabbed King Gaeil through. How many of them were by Aslan hands?",
        "tag": "name",
        "value": "Earl of Warwick"
    },
    {
        "text": "Not to mention the Draco king fleeing the royal capital after, fate unknown. And the Kingdom of Tara without its ruler was subjugated under Victorian sovereign authority, as if a matter of course.",
        "tag": "name",
        "value": "Earl of Warwick"
    },
    {
        "text": "I presume it wasn't his own subjects who prevented the Draco's return to the city.",
        "tag": "name",
        "value": "Earl of Warwick"
    },
    {
        "tag": "character",
        "name": "avg_npc_727_1#8$1"
    },
    {
        "text": "This is why I very much enjoy your works based on the Tarans' own ballads. You've led the people to see more of history's truth.",
        "tag": "name",
        "value": "Earl of Warwick"
    },
    {
        "tag": "character",
        "name": "avg_npc_239"
    },
    {
        "text": "Thank you for your appreciation.",
        "tag": "name",
        "value": "Plain-Dressed Bard"
    },
    {
        "text": "To write this story, I saw plays performed in the country, and paid a visit to some wandering minstrels who'd inherited the Taran tradition.",
        "tag": "name",
        "value": "Plain-Dressed Bard"
    },
    {
        "text": "\u2014But what struck me most wasn't the endangerment of Taran culture. It was how so many lives were just slipping away.",
        "tag": "name",
        "value": "Plain-Dressed Bard"
    },
    {
        "text": "Perhaps you believe the Tarans' ideal nation, and a border with Victoria, are necessary for the Taran people to be saved.",
        "tag": "name",
        "value": "Plain-Dressed Bard"
    },
    {
        "text": "But I think, if we ourselves can live better, if we can plant seeds of ideas for the many Tarans who can't read...",
        "tag": "name",
        "value": "Plain-Dressed Bard"
    },
    {
        "text": "Won't we have won then and there, against the Victorians who want us trapped in ignorance and poverty all our lives?",
        "tag": "name",
        "value": "Plain-Dressed Bard"
    },
    {
        "tag": "dialog"
    },
